--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relationship to the private instance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository is the PUBLIC RELEASE of SkynetClaw. It is assembled from the
author's private working instance by an explicit allowlist, and deliberately
excludes:

  * the operator's personal profile prompt (backend/prompts/USER.md) -- a
    template is provided at backend/prompts/USER.example.md
  * the operator's Obsidian vault memory, council archives, and session
    checkpoints
  * all runtime state: databases, indexes, session logs, generated SELF.md
  * machine-specific scripts and generated reports

Nothing here is a record of anyone's private work. The vault directory that
ships with this repository contains architecture and theory documents only, and
is intended as a STARTER TEMPLATE for your own vault.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this software is, and is not
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SkynetClaw runs autonomous agents that can read and write files, execute tools,
and reach the network. That is the point of it, and it is also the risk.

  * It is NOT sandboxed by default. Run it against a workspace you are willing
    to lose, and read the governance configuration before enabling execution.
  * The GPS-2 permission gate is deny-by-default and irreversible actions
    require a human gate. Do not disable those unless you fully understand the
    consequence -- they are what makes autonomy survivable.
  * Model output is not verified truth. The Reality Grading loop grades claims
    against evidence precisely because a model's own account of its success
    cannot be trusted.

You are responsible for what you let it do.

